{%- comment -%}
  Where to find Wear Label off this site — Instagram, Shopee, TikTok.

  Asked for 2026-09-27 with the three URLs and a question about placement: "ini
  apply dimana ya? gw kepikiran di home sama di about, or u got better ideas?"
  The answer this section implements is home AND About AND the footer, which is
  three places for one reason each rather than the same reason three times:

  - **The footer** is the baseline. It is on every page, it is where a reader
    who is already looking for a social link looks first, and it costs nothing.
    It renders the compact row variant.
  - **The home page** is where the reader who is NOT looking for it is. This
    section replaced `instagram-strip` in the ready-to-wear view, and that swap
    is the argument for placing it here at all: the strip was headed "Follow us
    on Instagram" and was in fact a marquee of the catalogue's own product
    photos with no link on any of them, eight of eleven tiles drawing grey
    placeholders because eight products have no photograph. It promised a
    destination and went nowhere. This does the job the strip was pretending to
    do. `instagram-strip` is still in the repo and still correct — it is
    unplaced, like `category-mosaic` and `hero-carousel`, and putting it back
    is one edit to templates/index.json plus a block in `home-tabs`.
  - **The About page** is where a reader has just finished reading about the
    studio and has nowhere to go next. The page deliberately has no CTA (see
    `about-story.liquid`), and three links out are not a CTA.

  THE LINKS THEMSELVES LIVE IN THEME SETTINGS, not here — see
  `snippets/social-links.liquid` for why, and note the consequence: this section
  has no URL fields of its own and adding one here would be the bug that
  snippet exists to prevent.

  THE SECTION REMOVES ITSELF when every URL is blank. The heading is not
  rendered either: a heading over nothing is worse than an absent band, and
  unlike a product photograph there is no layout here that depends on the
  missing thing, so this is not a placeholder case. `custom-hero` makes the same
  call for the same reason.

  NO BACKGROUND COLOUR, deliberately. The cards are `bg-canvas` on the page's
  own `--color-ground`, with the marks on `bg-surface` inside them — the design
  system's three-deep surface stack used as intended. On the home page this
  lands directly under the voices wall, which is espresso; on About it lands
  under the statement band, which is Camel. A third coloured band against
  either would be two coloured bands touching.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign has_any = false
  if settings.social_instagram_url != blank or settings.social_shopee_url != blank or settings.social_tiktok_url != blank
    assign has_any = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if has_any -%}
  <section aria-labelledby="social-heading" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-7 px-gutter py-section">
    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 id="social-heading" class="font-display text-h2">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
      </h2>
      <p class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body, label: 'body', lines: 2 %}
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The card grid is NOT inside the `data-reveal` above. The reveal animates
      opacity, which makes its element a stacking context — harmless here today,
      and exactly the trap this repo has hit three times when something with a
      blend or a transform ended up inside one. Keeping the grid out costs
      nothing and removes the question.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% render 'social-links', variant: 'cards' %}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Elsewhere",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The three destination links come from Theme settings → Social, not from here, because the footer and two pages all render the same three and must not be three places to edit. With all three blank this whole section is not rendered."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Find us elsewhere" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "New pieces, restocks and what the studio is working on — posted as it happens. Shopee is where you can buy from us on the marketplace you already use." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Elsewhere" }]
}
{% endschema %}
